---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About — SHINYA / 深夜">
  <div class="container">
    <section class="section prose">
      <h2 style="font-size: 0.85rem; letter-spacing: 0.4em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--neon-purple);">About</h2>
      <h1 style="font-family: var(--font-jp); letter-spacing: 0.15em;">深夜 — SHINYA</h1>
      <p style="font-family: var(--font-jp); color: var(--text-dim);">夜はまだ長い。— The night is still long.</p>
      <p>
        SHINYA (深夜, "late night" in Japanese) is a music project for the hours after midnight —
        when the city goes quiet, the neon stays on, and everything sounds a little more honest.
      </p>
      <p>
        The sound lives somewhere between a Tokyo jazz kissa at 1am, an empty city pop street in 1985,
        and the lofi hum of a desk lamp at 3. Original tracks and long-form mixes are made for
        thinking, driving, working, and the kind of nights when you don't really want to sleep yet.
      </p>
      <p>
        New music arrives on
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@shinyatokyo" target="_blank" rel="noopener">YouTube</a> —
        always at midnight.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
